CLAIM: CUB lateroll@29 achieves 81.39% at 12.99 GFLOPs/image on final seeds 1–3, with positive paired 95% CIs against all six K=29 baselines; gains over maskedkd, rollout and tome remain below the promotion threshold.
VERDICT: NEEDS-MORE
REASON: The reported numbers match the supplied metrics and Core comparison, but final_lateroll_k29_s1_1101_104303_ef38, final_lateroll_k29_s2_1101_125958_6470 and final_lateroll_k29_s3_1101_140937_ec98—and their maskedkd counterparts—have digests differing from the current lock. Rule 3 is unsatisfied; historical lock verification and authenticated change details are missing, as are the other baselines’ metrics needed to verify epochs and integrity.
The truncated H-C2b evidence omits the cited summary/verdict and PROPOSALS/commit records establishing analysis completion before implementation. Supply those records. Novelty is weak: the source implements a depth-restricted variant of [attention rollout](https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.385/); the acknowledged sub-threshold differences do not establish a meaningful research win.